    from outlets o, (values
      ('Trump Pairs Allied Investment Pledges With Midterm Campaign Events, Analysis Says', '• Analysis piece from The Diplomat; no author name appears in the extracted text, so the article is attributed to the outlet.
• Source refers only to “Trump”/“the president”; first name deliberately not added.
• Investment figures ($54B Alaska, $22B Texas, up to $120B nuclear) are U.S.-announced headline numbers; Seoul has not confirmed them.
• Nov. 3 is cited in the source as a benchmark date before the election; verify if used elsewhere.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/us-economic-diplomacy-with-allies-becomes-an-election-showcase-for-trump/
• Photo: roger4336 / Flickr (CC BY-SA 2.0) — https://www.flickr.com/photos/24736216@N07/3824994628 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('India Confirms Akash Air Defense Exports to Tajikistan and Turkmenistan', '• Neither Tajikistan nor Turkmenistan has confirmed the purchases; confirmation is from Indian officials and ANI only.
• Source spells the Tajik capital “Dushnabe” (typo); article uses Dushanbe.
• No quantities, prices or delivery dates are public; do not add any.
• Singh''s remarks were made in ''early October'' per source; exact date not given.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/tajikistan-turkmenistan-to-import-indian-surface-to-air-missile-systems/
• Photo: Ank Kumar / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=121587301 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('Pakistan Tests Longer-Range Fatah-IV Cruise Missile, Commentary Weighs Motives', '• OPINION/ANALYSIS: commentary written from a clearly Pakistani perspective; no author name in the extracted text. Article is framed as a summary of the author''s argument.
• Claims about Indian jet losses on May 6-7, 2025, are contested and attributed to the author only.
• The ~1,000 km range is the author''s estimate from imagery; the reported test range is ''more than 750 km.''
• No Indian government response in source; consider seeking one before publication.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/why-pakistan-tested-an-extended-range-version-of-the-fatah-iv/
• Photo: Skybolt101 at English Wikipedia / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=21818273 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('Pakistan Imposes Emergency and Governor''s Rule in PTI-Run Khyber Pakhtunkhwa', '• Source is news analysis; interpretive lines are attributed to The Diplomat.
• Source says Tarar spoke ''on Sunday'' and Kundi ''on Monday''; converted to Oct. 11 and Oct. 12 (2026 calendar checked).
• District list reproduced as in source (''both Upper and South Waziristan''); verify official naming.
• Allegation of PTI-militant ''nexus'' is a government claim; PTI denies it.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/pakistan-imposes-emergency-and-governors-rule-in-khyber-pakhtunkhwa/
• Photo: Mohammed Ahmed Arsalan Khan / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=72894651 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('U.S. Freezes Green Card Sponsorship by Eight Tech Firms, Straining Ties With India', '• Source inconsistency: the dek says H-1B visa applications were blocked, but the body describes a suspension from PERM (green card labor certification). Article follows the body.
• Source says the move ''covers four leading Indian IT firms'' (Srivastava) without naming which; Cognizant and Capgemini are not described as Indian in the source, so the article avoids a precise count of Indian firms.
• Timing of Rubio visit: source says both ''weeks before'' and ''later this month''; article uses ''later this month.''
• Act name spelled both ''Lindsey'' and ''Lindsay'' in the source; verify official title.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/trumps-targeting-of-indian-it-firms-hits-india-us-ties-again/
• Photo: Zondor at English Wikipedia / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 3.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=12796125 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('Rahul Gandhi Leads Mass March in Delhi as Protests Over Election Chief Grow', '• Source uses strongly critical language (''brutal crackdown'', ''city under siege''); article tones this down and attributes characterizations.
• Crowd sizes, detention numbers and the 30,000 deployment figure are from the source only; no official figures given.
• Police brutality allegations are unverified claims by protesters.
• Weekdays checked: Saturday = Oct. 10, Monday = Oct. 12 (2026).
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/protests-escalate-in-delhi-despite-modi-governments-heavy-handed-crackdown/
• Photo: Wikimedia Commons / Wikimedia Commons (CC0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=175809079 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('Malaysia to Press ASEAN Ministers on Haze Crisis Ahead of Manila Summit', '• Source says Mohamad Hasan spoke ''yesterday'' relative to an Oct. 13 (KST) publication; exact date not certain, so no date given.
• Source quotes ''Environment Minister Hanif Faisol Nurofiq'' on the Jakarta center without naming his country; omitted from the article to avoid assumption.
• Final paragraph summarizes The Diplomat''s analysis, not a government position.
• Indonesian aircraft numbers (3-4 planes, 34 helicopters) are as relayed by Malaysia''s foreign minister via Bernama.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/malaysia-to-raise-transboundary-haze-crisis-with-asean-foreign-ministers-ahead-of-summit/
• Photo: Firdaus Latif / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 2.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=30750080 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('South Korea Recalls Envoy to Ukraine, Demands Apology Over POW Transfer Disclosure', '• Source mixes news with analysis (e.g., ''badly miscalculated''); evaluative lines omitted, Seoul''s three demands attributed to The Diplomat.
• Source identifies Kyrylo Budanov as ''head of the Ukrainian presidential office''; kept with attribution, verify title.
• The Japan territorial claim reference (2008 Dokdo recall) is as stated in source.
• Vlasiuk''s fuel-shipment claim is disputed by Seoul.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/south-korea-recalls-ambassador-demands-public-apology-from-ukraine/
• Photo: Republic of Korea from Seoul, Republic of Korea / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 2.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=167127787 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('EU to Cap Chinese Hybrid Vehicle Imports at 350,000 a Year Under New Deal', '• Source headline says ''hybrid'' but body cites 800,000 ''battery and plug-in hybrids''; confirm exactly which vehicle categories the quota covers.
• Think tank name given as ''European Council for Foreign Relations'' in source; verify (likely European Council on Foreign Relations).
• ''On Thursday'' refers to the week of the Oct. 12 article (likely Oct. 15); kept as weekday.
• Trade deficit figure is given in pounds in the source; not converted.
• Source (The Guardian): https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/12/eu-deal-china-limit-imports-hybrid-electric-vehicles
• Photo: KenSwe72 / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY 4.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=191799123 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('Malaysia''s Anwar Hosts Myanmar''s Min Aung Hlaing, Backs Return to ASEAN Fold', '• Source dated Oct. 8 (KST); ''today'' in source taken as Oct. 8, Malaysia time. Older than other items in batch.
• Source typo: says Min Aung Hlaing ''arrived in Myanmar''; context makes clear he arrived in Malaysia.
• Source garbles the BROUK appeal (''order Myanmar''s arrest''); article says the group urged Anwar to have him detained.
• Anwar''s quote is cleaned of invisible zero-width characters present in the extracted source text.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/in-a-diplomatic-shift-malaysian-pm-hosts-myanmars-min-aung-hlaing/
• Photo: Lula Oficial / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=177906966 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('Japan''s Non-Nuclear Principles Face Fresh Scrutiny Ahead of New Security Strategy', '• Analysis piece (The Diplomat, Tokyo Report); author is not named in the extracted text, so the story attributes arguments to ''the analysis''. Verify byline.
• Japanese names kept in family-name-first order as in the source (Takaichi Sanae, Sato Eisaku, Okada Katsuya).
• SLCM-N deployment on attack submarines is described in the source as expected but not officially confirmed.
• The ''end of 2026'' timing for the new National Security Strategy comes from the source.
• Source (The Diplomat): https://thediplomat.com/2026/10/whither-japans-three-non-nuclear-principles/
• Photo: Cabinet Public Affairs Office, Cabinet Secretariat / Wikimedia Commons (CC BY 4.0) — https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=76721345 (keep the credit line)
• Rewritten from published reporting with attribution. Verify facts against the original before major edits.'),
      ('Writers Argue Kim Jong Un Stands to Gain From a Fourth Summit With Trump', '• OPINION piece: written as the authors'' imagined Foreign Ministry advice to Kim. Authors are not named in the extracted text (first-person plural), so the story says ''the authors''. Verify byline before publishing.
• Characterizations of Trump''s age, health and personality are the authors'' views framed as a hypothetical North Korean assessment; keep clearly attributed.
